# Concepts

Wyrd has a small vocabulary. Four nouns cover the whole system:

| Noun | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| **Card** | The typed, versioned envelope for one AI system component. |
| **Spec** | The kind-specific payload inside a card. One JSON Schema per `kind`. |
| **Run** | An execution record: the agent or workflow that ran, the inputs, the outputs, and the trace. |
| **Observation** | A derived record — drift signal, eval score, or audit entry — attached to a card or run. |

## How they relate

A `Card` carries a `Spec`. A `Spec` can hold `CardRef`s to other cards — the
server derives the lineage graph from them. A `Run` records what executed and
which cards drove it. `Observations` annotate cards and runs with evidence.

This is the mental model section. For a component workflow, use the [Cards
hub](/cards/), [Bifrost](/bifrost/), or [How-to guides](/how-to/) instead.

